      "b": "📢 SSN Upload Failure – Verification Process Update for Tax Purposes**\n\nHey team! \n\nWe have started collecting **Social Security Numbers (SSNs)** from eligible members for tax purposes. As a result, we may encounter members who fail their SSN upload attempts and receive an error message.\n\nPlease follow the updated process below when assisting these members:\n\n**What agents need to do:**\n\n1. **DO NOT send Secondary Doc V** for SSN verification, even if the member encounters an SSN upload error.\n2. Send the regular **Doc V** instead, asking the member to upload a valid **ID or passport**.\n3. Once the member completes the ID/passport upload, **tag Lead Assist (LA)** to request a reset of the member's SSN upload attempts through Backoffice.\n\n**Important Reminders:**\n- Do not send Secondary Doc V specifically for SSN upload failures.\n- The member only needs to complete the regular ID/passport verification process.\n- LA will handle resetting the member's SSN upload attempts through Backoffice.\n\nPlease make sure everyone is aligned with this updated workflow to avoid sending the wrong verification request. Thank you! 🙌",
